WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.339
so for anybody in my audience who maybe, just
maybe was getting slightly complacent about

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:12.120
the November presidential election because
the polls just look so good for Joe Biden,

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.760
this is a red alert moment for you.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.790
It should be a wakeup call to every one of
us that nothing is over.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.080
This is going to be a huge fight.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.590
Donald Trump could certainly win.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.960
We could be facing four more years of a Trump
presidency, according to data provided to

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:32.219
Axios by, yes, the Trump campaign and the
RNC.

00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:39.819
Republicans have more registered voters than
Democrats in some key states relative to 2016.

00:00:39.819 --> 00:00:46.059
And I'll tell you, I've looked at the data
and it's a mess now as a pretext, not as a

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:48.670
pretext, as a as as a disclaimer.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.820
I think better said they may be lying.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.879
So I'm going to give you the data that Axios
was given by the Trump campaign and by the

00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:59.679
RNC about voter registration.

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:01.549
They could be lying if they're lying.

00:01:01.549 --> 00:01:02.549
Great.

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:03.549
Then we'll win by a lot.

00:01:03.549 --> 00:01:04.549
Okay.

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:06.210
But if they're not lying, we need to take
this seriously.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.210
And that's why this matters.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.460
So the point here is.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:16.130
All we can do because we don't know what the
truth is, is register every voter, convince

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.040
every voter to vote.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.619
Make sure every vote is counted.

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:21.360
We've got to work on this at all levels.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.360
But here is what was given to Axios by the
Trump campaign and the RNC compared to the

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.329
numbers that Axios was given by the Democratic
Party.

00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:31.700
And if this is wrong.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.700
Great.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.159
But we have to, at least for now, assume that
this is accurate.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:45.090
In Florida, the Democratic registration advantage
over Republicans was reduced by 87000 registered

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.130
voters since 2016.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.420
Now think back to 2016.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.850
Trump won Florida by one hundred and twelve
thousand votes.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:02:00.969
If indeed now the party registration advantage
for Democrats has shrunk by nearly 90000 voters,

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:02.780
that is almost twice.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:08.100
That is almost equivalent to that would almost
double Donald Trump's victory margin in 2016.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.030
However, new registrations are favoring Democrats.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.250
So what this means is you've had people who
move in and out of the state.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.420
People who switch party, et cetera.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.090
Among simply new registrations, Democrats
are winning.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:27.260
But when you account for all of the other
changes in registration, Democrats have actually

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.280
fallen behind in Florida.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.090
OK, Pennsylvania.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:36.380
Pennsylvania is a state that Donald Trump
won by 44000 in 2016.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:43.210
And the Democratic advantage in voter registration
has been reduced by one hundred and thirty

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:46.430
three thousand voters since 2016.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:52.400
Again, Trump won by 44000 Democrats relative
to Republicans have lost one hundred and thirty

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.210
three thousand voters since 2016.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.430
Important among new registrations.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.130
Democrats have a 15 point advantage.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:07.820
But again, because of moving deaths, a changing
of party, etc., the advantage has been reduced

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.290
by one hundred thirty three thousand.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:16.510
In Arizona, Republicans have taken the advantage
in registered voters over Democrats in Iowa.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.150
Republicans have taken advantage and registered
voters over Democrats.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:24.570
And in North Carolina, the Democratic net
advantage has shrunk.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:29.870
This is why overwhelming the vote is the necessary
action here.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:33.340
If they're going to suppress the vote, well,
let's overwhelm the vote so that suppressing

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.300
it point o five point five or one percent
won't make a difference.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.570
They win over.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:43.480
They win over Democrats in terms of new registrations
or in terms of people who overwhelm the ballot

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.480
box.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.480
Right.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.500
It is truly the solution here to all of the
problems.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:55.540
Now, another really important thing when you
look at new registrations and see the Democratic

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.540
advantage.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:03.200
So, for example, imagine that in a certain
state, the Republicans were able to increase

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:08.070
their advantage in terms of party registration
by 100000.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:14.190
But among new voters who were never previously
registered, Democrats registered more new

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.190
people.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:22.060
My guess is that the new registrants are more
likely to vote because something got them

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.870
to register since the last election.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.590
So maybe that's in our in our corner to our
advantage.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.240
But you can't assume anything.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.330
Now, there are a few funny caveats here, but
again, they shouldn't change our behavior.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:40.600
Number one, some of the people changing registration
to the Republican Party, they might be doing

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.550
it in order to mess with the Republican Party.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:47.960
We've seen people switch to the Democratic
Party to vote in the Democratic primary, even

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.620
though they have no intention of actually
voting for the Democrat in a general election.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.100
We've seen it the other way.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.230
We don't know for sure.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:58.490
But it is possible that there are people switching
to Republican registration for a variety of

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.790
different reasons, many of which might not
mean they are necessarily voting for Trump

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:02.790
in November.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.790
We don't know.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:04.790
We can't do anything about it.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:12.630
And again, we are evaluating registration
based on the data given to Axios by the Trump

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.850
campaign and the Republican Party.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:15.850
They could be lying.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:16.850
They lie all the time.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.060
It wouldn't be hugely surprising if they were
lying.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.790
But we can't know that right now and we won't
know it until the election.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.790
If at all.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.980
So we can't act on that basis.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.310
All we can act on.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:34.440
All that we should be motivated to do is to
keep going and assume nothing going into November.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.990
Every single voter I apologize.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.180
I know I say this a lot.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:45.400
Every single voter should act as if their
vote could turn your state from one candidate

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.400
to the other.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.680
That's how I will be voting in Massachusetts,
although certainly mathematically it's not

00:05:49.680 --> 00:06:51.300
going to be

00:06:51.300 --> 00:07:02.480
the case.

